 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+
+## Browser agent tools
+
+In browsers with WebMCP enabled in a secure context, every page exposes
+`search-articles` (`query`), `get-reading-list` (no arguments), and
+`toggle-article-bookmark` (`slug`). Search opens the search panel; bookmark
+changes update open reading-list panels and the current article bookmark.
+Tools use the current browser session and respect the configured base URL.
+
+The search panel also exposes `search-articles-form` through a normal HTML
+form. The reading-list panel exposes `remove-reading-list-article-form`, and
+article bookmark forms expose `toggle-current-article-bookmark-form`. These
+forms return results to agent callers without navigating, and remain usable
+by people in browsers without WebMCP.
+
+Article pages expose these additional read-only request utilities:
+
+| Article | Tool | Arguments |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `silent-architects` | `get-plant-stats` | None |
+| `coastal-pulse` | `get-tide-levels` | None |
+| `coffee-alchemy` | `get-coffee-brew` | None |
+| `super-bowl-lx` | `get-article-popularity` | `id` |
+
+Request utilities return status, redirect information, and response data,
+including errors from the demonstration endpoints. The existing article
+network demonstrations remain in place. The React WebMCP integration feature
+detects support and unregisters tools when their components unmount during
+navigation; requests forward agent cancellation signals.
